## 💡 Key Takeaways & Trade-offs

* **The Bias-Variance Balance:** Machine learning engineering requires a deliberate compromise. Selecting a model that is too simple leads to structural blindness (High Bias), while selecting a model that is too complex leads to noise memorization (High Variance).
* **The Diagnostic Power of Learning Curves:** Simply looking at a perfect training error score is deceptive. Plotting cross-validated performance against dataset scale changes is the most reliable method for catching overfitting before deploying models to production.

